{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"command -v cljstyle; command -v clj-kondo; cat .cljstyle 2>/dev/null | head -60; sed -n '145,165p' test/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc; sed -n '355,382p' test/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc; tail -6 target/nightly-repl-jvm.log; tail -8 target/nightly-python-jvm.log\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/cljstyle/0.17.642/cljstyle\n;; :namespaces is disabled project-wide. It rewrites ns forms, which is\n;; unsafe on this multi-platform codebase in two distinct ways:\n;; 1. ClojureDart uses string-prefixed :import forms (e.g.\n;;    (:import [\"dart:core\" BigInt DateTime])); the rule rewrites these\n;;    into JVM-style forms, which the cljd compiler then fails to resolve.\n;; 2. .cljc files that guard a JVM-only :import/:require clause with\n;;    #?(:cljd nil :clj ...) rely on :cljd appearing FIRST (the cljd\n;;    host-eval pass also matches :clj, so first-match-wins order is\n;;    load-bearing — see the reader-conditional trap in project memory).\n;;    The rule reorders reader-conditional branches alphabetically\n;;    (:clj before :cljd), silently re-breaking the guard on every\n;;    `cljstyle fix` — this bit dao.jing.dht.node.cljc and cost a lost\n;;    commit before being traced back here.\n{:files {:extensions #{\"blog\" \"chp\" \"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljd\" \"cljs\" \"edn\" \"jolt\"},\n         :ignore #{\".cpcache\" \".git\" \".shadow-cljs\" \"node_modules\" \"target\"}},\n :rules {:blank-lines {:enabled? true, :max-consecutive 2},\n         :eof-newline {:enabled? true},\n         :indentation {:enabled? true},\n         :namespaces {:enabled? false},\n         :whitespace\n           {:enabled? true, :insert-missing? true, :remove-trailing? true}}}\n  [pk hook-prelude prep]\n  (on-every-vm (hooks/program hook-prelude\n                              (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n                                (tree-of (:derived (derive* pk hooks/profile)))))\n               prep\n               outcome))\n\n\n(defn- every=\n  [expected results]\n  (doseq [[k result] results]\n    (is (= expected result) (str k))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Marks\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(declare nodes)\n\n\n   composition serves both modules.\"\n  ([ast] (on-every-vm ast []))\n  ([ast signals]\n   (into {}\n         (map (fn [k]\n                [k (try (outcome (h/run-linked\n                                   k ast\n                                   {:link-source (h/safepoint-source),\n                                    :prep (with-signals signals)}))\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n                          [:thrown (ex-message e)]))]))\n         (keys h/backends))))\n\n\n(defn- every=\n  [expected results]\n  (doseq [[k result] results]\n    (is (= expected result) (str k))))\n\n\n(defn- linked-run\n  \"The wrapped derived program of `pk` on every VM under `signals`.\"\n  [pk signals]\n  (on-every-vm (hooks/linked-program (derived-ast pk)) signals))\n\n\n(defn- linked-traced-run\n  \"The wrapped derived program of `pk` under the linked tracing profile.\"\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.repl.main-test\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
